This directory holds the copyright and license notice of musl libc, unchanged.

vow-run and the test programs are linked statically against musl, so a binary that is passed on contains
parts of it, and the MIT license of musl asks that its copyright notice and permission notice go with
every copy of those parts. COPYRIGHT is that notice, byte for byte, from the musl 1.2.6 release:

  source   https://musl.libc.org/releases/musl-1.2.6.tar.gz
  sha256   d585fd3b613c66151fc3249e8ed44f77020cb5e6c1e635a616d3f9f82460512a  (the tarball)
  file     musl-1.2.6/COPYRIGHT

The kiss package installs it as /usr/share/licenses/vow/musl-COPYRIGHT. It describes musl 1.2.6, the
version this machine builds with; dist/kiss/vow/build warns if the musl it finds is another version, and
then this file has to be replaced by the COPYRIGHT of that release. The files in this directory are not
covered by the licenses of vow: musl is MIT, with the notices that COPYRIGHT lists for parts of it.
